<title>FRANCE: Algeria's insurance firm CAAR posts $6.9 mln profi.</title>
<headline>Algeria's insurance firm CAAR posts $6.9 mln profi.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's main insurance firm, state-owned Algerian Insurance and Reinsurance Company (CAAR) posted a 376.34 million dinars ($6.9 million) net profit in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>APS, which gave no comparative figure, said CAAR had a turnover of 9.62 billion dinars ($178 million) in 1995.</p>
<p>CAAR is involved in a broad range of insurance business related to trade, industry, banks, ports, transport and hotels. ($ = 54 dinars)</p>
</text>
